<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-CPR-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-CPR-001" ;
  triage:title "AC 8's literal RULE-003 gate command is broken for both files it names" ;
  triage:description "AC 8's awk one-liner (match on the first line starting with a cfg(test) attribute, exit, count lines, fail above 1000) exits at the first #[cfg(test)] attribute: herdr_queue_wake.rs:26 (`#[cfg(test)] use tokio::sync::Notify;`) and herdr_escalation.rs:8, long before `mod tests`, so it counts ~25 and ~8 lines and always passes. The authoritative gate .just/check_line_counts.py is correct (herdr_queue_wake.rs 997/1000 at head c9e8bf3af) and unaffected. Remediation: replace the awk command in AC 8 with `python3 .just/check_line_counts.py` (the RULE-003 authority) and delete the hand-rolled one-liner anywhere else in docs/plans/phase-ax/." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
